# Added 2026-09-13 (Sam) after discovering every SHA-256 hash pinned in this repo's
# frozen/accepted artifacts (R04 accounting fixtures, A11 evidence/occurrences) was
# computed against a Windows working tree with core.autocrlf=true, which silently
# converts LF to CRLF on checkout. Git's actual stored blob is LF-normalized, so a
# fresh clone (or any machine without that specific local autocrlf setting) produces
# different bytes -- and therefore a different SHA-256 -- than the one pinned in the
# acceptance docs, even though the content is identical. This forces every checkout,
# on every machine, to use the same (LF) line endings for these text formats, so a
# SHA-256 of a locally-checked-out file always matches the committed blob.
* text=auto eol=lf
